          "args": "(struct printbuf *p, const char *msg,...)",
          "brief": "\n        ",
          "definition": "int sprintbuf",
          "detailed": "Formatted print to printbuf.\nThis function is the most expensive of the available functions for appending string data to a printbuf and should be used only where convenience is more important than speed. Avoid using this function in high performance code or tight loops; in these scenarios, consider using snprintf() with a static buffer in conjunction with one of the printbuf_*append() functions.\nSee also: printbuf_memappend_fast() printbuf_memappend() printbuf_strappend()",
